@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Candidate logical revision and protected-reference model
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

class ProfileRevision {
 exact reusable content identity
}
class ResumeDraft {
 independent selection / order / overrides
 expected version / source provenance
}
class PublicationManifest <<immutable>> {
 exact content / language / layout
}
class PublicationPointer {
 reviewed live scope / version
}
class SubmissionEvent {
 actual occurrence / capture completeness
}
class ActualMaterialManifest {
 exact submitted material provenance
}
class ProtectedArtifactReference {
 consumer namespace / resource / revision
 purpose / protection state
}
class Artifact {
 canonical identity / actual usability
}
ResumeDraft --> ProfileRevision : compared source provenance
ResumeDraft --> PublicationManifest : separate confirmed publication
PublicationPointer --> PublicationManifest : current revision
SubmissionEvent --> ActualMaterialManifest : actual captured set
PublicationManifest --> ProtectedArtifactReference : published evidence
ActualMaterialManifest --> ProtectedArtifactReference : historical material
ProtectedArtifactReference --> Artifact : guards reclamation
note bottom of ResumeDraft
 Source edits never auto-apply.
 Mutable source links cannot reconstruct history.
end note
note bottom of Artifact
 Exact bytes may be shared safely by identity.
 Existence grants no retrieval authority.
 Reference/deletion race needs concrete coordination.
end note
@enduml
